  "generated_text": "1. **Rotation**: A $45^\\circ$ rotation around the origin in the counter-clockwise direction can be achieved by multiplying the complex number by $e^{i\\pi/4} = \\frac{1+i}{\\sqrt{2}}$.\n   \\[\n   (-3 - 8i) \\cdot \\frac{1+i}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{-3 - 8i - 3i - 8i^2}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{-3 - 11i + 8}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{5 - 11i}{\\sqrt{2}}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Dilation**: A dilation centered at the origin with scale factor $\\sqrt{2}$ multiplies the complex number by $\\sqrt{2}$.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{5 - 11i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{2} = 5 - 11i\n   \\]\n\nThus, the resulting complex number after both transformations is $5 - 11i$.\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{5 - 11i}$.",
  "grade": {
